  "design": [
    "Core allows optional actual per-ShadowRealm host initialization and owns/traces the returned formatter value in Error realm intrinsics.",
    "Node executes unchanged configured primordials/internal-errors modules in each ShadowRealm; the default hook, private brand, override WeakMap and internal fallback are genuinely realm local.",
    "Private CJS process/require services are actual existing host objects, without exposing those globals. Existing ordinary CJS interop shim is byte-identical after factoring.",
    "Original-source positions are preserved through real wrapper line/UTF16 column offsets in the target realm.",
    "Custom prototypes/caller globals stay rooted across host initialization, collection and exceptions. Core test forces collection and checks both compiler modes."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Goal remains open. Latest complete stable1787/5015 and pinned1815/4727 are older b673 inventories; selected restored stack cases are not added to those totals.",
    "Six existing ShadowRealm family failures remain; one existing iterator broadcast cleanup timeout remains.",
    "First Core link failed from disk exhaustion before tests; actual failed temporary was hashed/reclaimed and completed audit checkout sparsified without changing HEAD or630 source hashes. Fresh retry654/654 is the qualifying result.",
    "No speed claim: fixed-work8valid/0clean.",
    "Core initial library check caught missing std::fs qualification and was corrected before build; raw check retained.",
    "First API run362/363 exposed incoming lazy public util initialization reading guest-replaced validators. Capturing original getCallSites policy before guest execution corrected the real regression; subsequent complete363/363 qualifies the final source. Core654 bytes unchanged after this Node-only correction."
  ],
